<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Indian workers fill Germany's labor gaps but face hurdles and risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224655415d28adc976055bf92749ef03c3fb92edf967fa4111c3d95e51d74ad0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882--78ecce9504e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of Indians working in Germany has grown rapidly in recent years. But many continue to face challenges in the labor market. Some also fall victim to recruitment scams, leaving them vulnerable to exploitation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Taiwan's closely watched local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f91a6a1f6fbce3baa8f68f3445a00c79d71f8d59d1ab87bb9c3813a37d6df2c</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T02:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polls-open-in-taiwan-s-closely-watched-local-elections/a-80083086--10a314bcb067.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/polls-open-in-taiwan-s-closely-watched-local-elections/a-80083086?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polls have opened for local elections in Taiwan. While campaigners have stayed away from the topic of China and focused on issues like transport and childcare, Beijing has repeatedly weighed in.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's Sanchez makes final appeal to voters before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:629b9afebe6852eb7e2112d11a9e52ea42cb2a94a6e6aedfd3daa38e5da71307</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T00:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-sanchez-makes-final-appeal-to-voters-before-election/a-80082783--097c77a9a9e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-sanchez-makes-final-appeal-to-voters-before-election/a-80082783?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez told people to turn out in large numbers so the country does not go "backwards." Polls suggest an end to his eight-year leftist leadership of Spain.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US disables ship in Gulf of Oman under Iran blockade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6cd3a1a952ca853133d7f2075f05d2135db0aafed840510ccfefbc1447e6b866</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T23:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-disables-ship-in-gulf-of-oman-under-iran-blockade/a-80082950--319498537e26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-disables-ship-in-gulf-of-oman-under-iran-blockade/a-80082950?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The United States said it was continuing "to strictly enforce the blockade" of Iran's ports. Meanwhile, Kuwait summoned Iran's ambassador over a strike that killed two Italian technicians.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Supreme Court largely upholds Quebec secularism bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a54250e9d54466f1dcc8f3517a528b09e41b949296e8064fde7caadc5df484</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T20:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571--e81b43653220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Quebec's government passed Bill 21 to ban religious symbols for public servants, arguing it was necessary to protect its secularist society. Critics argue the bill weakens legal protections for fundamental rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Lawmakers approve debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba0b765cb99034ab4d3cd4e2466d0bdecc2318ce8dfbf6b0998ebc5e5b8465c8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T19:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-lawmakers-approve-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-80071074--c798e4fa7b92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-lawmakers-approve-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-80071074?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers voted on a federal budget which foresees €556 billion in spending. Elsewhere, the Left Party is hosting a summit on femicide and the BSW party conference starts in Dresden. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish rider Marc Marquez announces MotoGP retirement, days after clinching record 8th world title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d90309fbbb115595a9268bd031252781da40f0449a48b578b644258b215da19</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T18:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930--3f20c4c08f5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-rider-marc-marquez-announces-motogp-retirement-days-after-clinching-record-8th-world-title/a-80079930?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marc Marquez took fans and his team by surprise when announcing this weekend's race in Valencia will be his last. The 33-year-old won a record eight MotoGP titles, including his rookie and retirement seasons.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France seeks German man in Channel migrant boat probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0984884c2c8f4956630bee9baa37e6b4e24aa45a25c8dbf08d8337a92ee7381e</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069--841769bf9248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-seeks-german-man-in-channel-migrant-boat-probe/a-80078069?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German businessman is accused of supplying equipment to smugglers organizing migrant crossings from France to the United Kingdom. However, he can't face formal charges until he is extradited to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Divisions deepen between EU member states after tense budget summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbffa5799e95e458cad14acb54568962626d578311bb94555f2bbb0ed678bde7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599--05a844bfc611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An EU leaders summit on the bloc's seven-year budget fell apart amid divisions over how to fund Ukraine. The budget proposal also includes a 3% tax on US tech companies, in a bid for the EU to generate additional funds.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kanal-Centre Pompidou, Brussels' most anticipated new art museum, opens its doors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acc9be5606e06fb5d1580e7637571d9bf2b190fba02845cfc9482c93d6b788e0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kanal-centre-pompidou-brussels-most-anticipated-new-art-museum-opens-its-doors/a-80001444--f96ce33fc4a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kanal-centre-pompidou-brussels-most-anticipated-new-art-museum-opens-its-doors/a-80001444?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major addition to Europe's cultural scene: Kanal-Centre Pompidou, the new contemporary art museum in a former Citroen factory complex, is celebrating its opening with a free, nonstop weekend program.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia's Student List runs chemistry professor Radomir Saicic for president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:176a350d909683fcfddb0ef9f2ed7d072df7aaf1689512c7745f0e2fbcabafc1</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-student-list-runs-chemistry-professor-radomir-saicic-for-president/a-80078700--106ebec53e85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-student-list-runs-chemistry-professor-radomir-saicic-for-president/a-80078700?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After ousting strongman Aleksandar Vucic, Serbia's student movement has now nominated academic Radomir Saicic for the upcoming presidential vote. Saicic accused the "outgoing regime" of trying to collapse the state.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Dutch authorities seize 26 critically endangered turtles from luggage of passenger bound for Hong Kong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9a7b24c586015ada5ec82b6bd5cf0702bd14ed5202df6776ce0332665288de5</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-ko/a-80077824--bdef9f0677e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-kong/a-80077824?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tiny Vallarta mud turtle was only discovered in 2018. It's critically endangered with around 300 thought to live in the wild. Almost one tenth of that number were stashed in a traveler's luggage, bound in duct tape.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Arsenic in the water: Thailand presses Myanmar over mining pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa06803aa098f3fbd94b35d377125497ab6784977d342f193616ba782a1c6f8</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295--98cdabbb5354.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thailand is seeking to tackle river pollution stemming from rare earth mines in neighboring Myanmar. The two countries held joint talks this week as a "first step towards agreeing on the evidence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Georgia: Police clash with Besiktas fans at Israel club game</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d05bd78c3700f3eb3018ff12fbe4387f720c063bf41e331a4f99ce0c6b1e164</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111--302857b88ba0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/georgia-police-clash-with-besiktas-fans-at-israel-club-game/a-80076111?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey's Besiktas accused Georgian police of using "disproportionate" force during the game with Israel's Hapoel Beer-Sheva, which saw Besiktas fans unfurl a banner supporting Palestine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airline Norse Atlantic files for bankruptcy, succumbing to aviation fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66bb245ae605a02785cd3ad1e9bcbc38f64146e3cde4c7ae2590d80536edc2fc</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728--deb84ffc1870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The low-cost airline was only founded a few years ago and had been struggling to turn a profit. The spike in aviation fuel prices caused by the war in Iran has now driven Norway's Norse Atlantic into bankruptcy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Gambia gears up for election, can Barrow secure a third term?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224cf44e96e709355587e05dba3150118991dc1abc9893f9abcec05bee09f6b5</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340--b6856a8ea5b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term as Gambians vote on December 5. The election will test the opposition's appeal and the country's progress on democratic reform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Informer TV owner Vucicevic arrested: Has the reckoning with Serbia's pro-Vucic media machine begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c5c380d08ebe2a149f1048430169d8d7790c9de22c94706e98301de87d0c4a9</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650--983ff7ae64ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of media owner Dragan J. Vucicevic raises questions about whether Serbia is holding the people behind the country's pro-Vucic media accountable — or whether this is another political power struggle.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte's ICC trial: What is at stake for the Philippines?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6357268099026c5e58938f58bc7102a4f9230a65105fe0350b39df26798f5755</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657--9d6c676a2419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte faces trial in The Hague over his deadly war on drugs. The proceedings could determine the political fortunes of a powerful dynasty. Victims' families hope to see justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Iran, child marriage risks complicated by war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e16630e0e91afcaadcffccd387c3880aba6ade70958f8b0c471c452e95dcb9be</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473--2a4ac067a146.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">War, poverty and disrupted schooling could put more girls in Iran at risk of child marriage, rights advocates have warned.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: VP Duterte says father's ICC case 'not a fair trial'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da7ba3a518a244c577d2f15b313151a722cc2d5f199cc0cd5cf89933949f6d90</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359--fe3a5d80492d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sara Duterte has said the ICC will not give her father a fair trial and that the Hague-based court wants to "make a statement." Duterte alleges the case against her father is politically motivated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The tiny BSW is a party in crisis, as it is set to hand the far-right AfD power in eastern Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99e88a8c7f11e870754f7295320b3d75716a4eaf3156646bbf52e796580d31fa</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417--98b542aa0047.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-tiny-bsw-is-a-party-in-crisis-as-it-is-set-to-hand-the-far-right-afd-power-in-eastern-germany/a-80074417?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sahra Wagenknecht's BSW party is set to disrupt German politics yet again. Espousing a mix of left-wing economic policy and populist far-right anti-migration rhetoric, it now stands to play kingmaker to the far right AfD</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
